// Stress test: 1000 planes across the same ten controller kinds and five
// airframes as stress_500. Each sector repeats its 500-plane controller mix,
// airspeeds, fuel fractions, formation slots, and trained RL envelope.
//
// Run headless (60 s of sim, one CSV sample per second per plane):
//   cargo run --release --example observe_state --no-default-features --features inference -- \
//     --scenario assets/scenarios/stress_1000.scenario.ron --steps 3840 --interval 64
// Without inference, the 68 RL planes are skipped, leaving 932 planes.
// Model files must be available at the paths used by stress_500.
//
// Layout: 2 sectors on a grid with 140 km between origins (five columns
// maximum). Spawn positions and orbit centers are translated together;
// sector-prefixed names keep wingmen and receivers linked to their own peers.
// Flight plans use absolute waypoints: every follower uses patrol.plan.ron
// near the world origin, so followers from other sectors fly toward that route
// and eventually share its terminal loiter. Manual planes descend to ground.
// As in stress_500, the load includes peer lookups, physics, controller updates,
// replication, and the HUD/map/roster; flight quality is not the objective.
//
// Controllers:
//   RlOrbit      36
//   RlLevelHold  32
//   Orbit        128
//   HeadingHold  112
//   LevelHold    358
//   Ascent       80
//   Wingman      204
//   Refueling    32
//   Manual       10
//   FlightPlan   8
(
    steps: 3840,
    interval: 64,
    planes: [
        // Sector 1: origin (0, 0) m.
